source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "train-vs-platform", "key_answer": "262 m"}, {"n": 15, "text": "If the surface area of a sphere increases by 69%, what is the percentage increase in its volume?", "options": [{"text": "90.3%", "added": false}, {"text": "138.6%", "added": false}, {"text": "119.7%", "added": false}, {"text": "103.5%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": "119.7%"}, {"n": 16, "text": "If the listed price of a bag is 76% more than its cost price and a discount of 54% is announced on it, then find the loss percentage.", "options": [{"text": "17.55%", "added": false}, {"text": "22.6%", "added": false}, {"text": "18.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "19.04%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": "19.04%"}, {"n": 17, "text": "The sum of the modes of the data sets {1, 7, 3, 7, 3, x} and {4, 8, 9, 8, 4, y} is 11. If x > y, then find the possible correct relation between x and y.", "options": [{"text": "x – y = 5", "added": false}, {"text": "x – y = 3", "added": false}, {"text": "x + y = 10", "added": false}, {"text": "x + y = 9", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Elementary Statistics", "sub": "mean-median-mode", "key_answer": "x – y = 3"}, {"n": 18, "text": "Prakhar and Riya together invested ₹56,700 in a business. At the end of the year, out of a total profit of ₹5,400, Prakhar's share was ₹1,400. What was Prakhar's investment?", "options": [{"text": "₹16,200", "added": false}, {"text": "₹14,900", "added": false}, {"text": "₹14,300", "added": false}, {"text": "₹14,700", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "partnership", "key_answer": "₹14,700"}, {"n": 19, "text": "If the height of a cylinder is 15 cm and its base area is 169π cm2, then find its